d{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3{b}_{1}+6{b}_{2}-2{b}_{3} \\\\  & =6{b}_{2}-2{b}_{3}+3{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-2(-3{b}_{2})-2{b}_{3}+3{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534532 17592186045417 true] [17592186424437 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424435 13194139534532 17592186045417 true] [17592186424437 1069 "q-113098" 13194139534532 17592186045417 true] [17592186424437 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534532 17592186045417 true] [17592186424437 1071 "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=-2{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=-2{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}?$" 13194139534532 17592186045417 true] [17592186424437 1072 #uuid "462a3ac8-3692-5123-988e-2869c674b5a5" 13194139534532 17592186045417 true] [17592186424437 1074 "We are given that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=-2{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}=-2{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{b}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{2}=-2{b}_{1}+(-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1})\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{4}{c}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-8{b}_{1}+6{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-8(-\\frac{1}{4}{c}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2})+6(-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}) \\\\  & =2{c}_{1}+4{c}_{2}-3{c}_{1} \\\\  & =-{c}_{1}+4{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534532 17592186045417 true] [17592186424438 1058 #edb/ref 17592186424441 13194139534532 17592186045417 true] [17592186424438 1062 #uuid "7799965b-8388-5cb7-a5d4-d8203068d7c5" 13194139534532 17592186045417 true] 